Relevant columns and how we will use them

• `event_date`           : restrict the analysis to 2‑Jan‑2021 (`'20210102'`).  
• `event_name`           : keep only *page_view* events.  
• `event_params`         : nested array that holds all GA4 parameters.  
    – we will pull the value of the parameter whose `key = 'page_location'`; that URL tells us which page was viewed.  
• (derived) `page_location` : the extracted URL string.  
• (derived) `parts`         : an ARRAY created by first stripping the protocol (`http/https`), then splitting the URL on `/`.  
• (derived) `page_type`     : flag a view as PDP, PLP, or OTHER with the rules that were supplied.  

Typical filter conditions we will re‑use  
```
WHERE event_date = '20210102'
  AND event_name = 'page_view'
```

--------------------------------------------------
Ten exploratory → final SQLs
(Each returns ≤ 20 rows except the final two that aggregate.)

```sql
-- 1. Quick look at raw rows for 2021‑01‑02
SELECT event_date, event_timestamp, event_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102`
WHERE event_date = '20210102'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Distinct event names on that day (verifies 'page_view' exists)
SELECT DISTINCT event_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102`
WHERE event_date = '20210102'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Peek inside event_params for a few page_view rows
SELECT ep.key,
       ep.value.string_value AS string_val,
       ep.value.int_value    AS int_val
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102`,
       UNNEST(event_params) AS ep
WHERE  event_date  = '20210102'
  AND  event_name  = 'page_view'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Pull the page_location parameter for 20 page views
SELECT
  (SELECT value.string_value
   FROM UNNEST(event_params)
   WHERE key = 'page_location') AS page_location
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102`
WHERE event_date = '20210102'
  AND event_name = 'page_view'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Show URL plus number of URL segments (after protocol)
SELECT
  page_location,
  ARRAY_LENGTH(SPLIT(REGEXP_REPLACE(page_location, r'^https?://', ''), '/')) AS n_segments
FROM (
  SELECT
    (SELECT value.string_value
     FROM UNNEST(event_params)
     WHERE key = 'page_location') AS page_location
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102`
  WHERE event_date = '20210102'
    AND event_name = 'page_view'
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Simple flag: does last segment contain '+' ?
SELECT
  page_location,
  parts[OFFSET(ARRAY_LENGTH(parts)-1)]             AS last_segment,
  IF(parts[OFFSET(ARRAY_LENGTH(parts)-1)] LIKE '%+%', 1, 0) AS has_plus
FROM (
  SELECT
    SPLIT(REGEXP_REPLACE(
             (SELECT value.string_value
              FROM UNNEST(event_params)
              WHERE key='page_location'),
             r'^https?://', ''), '/') AS parts
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102`
  WHERE event_date = '20210102'
    AND event_name = 'page_view'
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Bring in category test for 4th or 5th segment (case‑insensitive)
SELECT
  page_location,
  parts[SAFE_OFFSET(3)] AS seg4,
  parts[SAFE_OFFSET(4)] AS seg5,
  CASE
    WHEN ARRAY_LENGTH(parts) >= 5
     AND ( REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(parts[3]), r'(accessories|apparel|brands|campus collection|drinkware|electronics|google redesign|lifestyle|nest|new 2015 logo|notebooks journals|office|shop by brand|small goods|stationery|wearables)')
        OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(parts[4]), r'(accessories|apparel|brands|campus collection|drinkware|electronics|google redesign|lifestyle|nest|new 2015 logo|notebooks journals|office|shop by brand|small goods|stationery|wearables)')
         )
     AND parts[OFFSET(ARRAY_LENGTH(parts)-1)] LIKE '%+%' THEN 'PDP'
    ELSE 'non‑PDP'
  END AS page_type
FROM (
  SELECT
    (SELECT value.string_value
     FROM UNNEST(event_params)
     WHERE key = 'page_location') AS page_location,
    SPLIT(REGEXP_REPLACE(
           (SELECT value.string_value
            FROM UNNEST(event_params)
            WHERE key='page_location'), r'^https?://', ''), '/') AS parts
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102`
  WHERE event_date='20210102'
    AND event_name='page_view'
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Count total page_view rows (sanity check)
SELECT COUNT(*) AS total_page_views
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102`
WHERE event_date='20210102'
  AND event_name='page_view';
```

```sql
-- 9. Count PDP‑qualified page views (using the refined test)
WITH views AS (
  SELECT
    SPLIT(REGEXP_REPLACE(
           (SELECT value.string_value
            FROM UNNEST(event_params) WHERE key='page_location'), r'^https?://', ''), '/') AS parts
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102`
  WHERE event_date='20210102'
    AND event_name='page_view'
)
SELECT COUNT(*) AS pdp_views
FROM views
WHERE ARRAY_LENGTH(parts) >= 5
  AND ( REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(parts[3]), r'(accessories|apparel|brands|campus collection|drinkware|electronics|google redesign|lifestyle|nest|new 2015 logo|notebooks journals|office|shop by brand|small goods|stationery|wearables)')
     OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(parts[4]), r'(accessories|apparel|brands|campus collection|drinkware|electronics|google redesign|lifestyle|nest|new 2015 logo|notebooks journals|office|shop by brand|small goods|stationery|wearables)')
      )
  AND parts[OFFSET(ARRAY_LENGTH(parts)-1)] LIKE '%+%';
```

```sql
-- 10. Final query: percentage of page views on 2021‑01‑02 that were PDPs
WITH pageviews AS (
  SELECT
    SPLIT(REGEXP_REPLACE(
           (SELECT value.string_value
            FROM UNNEST(event_params) WHERE key='page_location'), r'^https?://', ''), '/') AS parts
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20210102`
  WHERE event_date='20210102'
    AND event_name='page_view'
), classified AS (
  SELECT
    CASE
      WHEN ARRAY_LENGTH(parts) >= 5
       AND ( REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(parts[3]), r'(accessories|apparel|brands|campus collection|drinkware|electronics|google redesign|lifestyle|nest|new 2015 logo|notebooks journals|office|shop by brand|small goods|stationery|wearables)')
          OR REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(parts[4]), r'(accessories|apparel|brands|campus collection|drinkware|electronics|google redesign|lifestyle|nest|new 2015 logo|notebooks journals|office|shop by brand|small goods|stationery|wearables)')
           )
       AND parts[OFFSET(ARRAY_LENGTH(parts)-1)] LIKE '%+%' THEN 'PDP'
      ELSE 'OTHER'
    END AS page_type
  FROM pageviews
)
SELECT
  ROUND( 100 * COUNTIF(page_type = 'PDP') / COUNT(*), 2) AS pct_page_views_pdp
FROM classified;
```

The tenth query returns the requested percentage of page views that qualify as PDP‑type pages on 2‑Jan‑2021.
